sequenceDiagram
    participant A as NA-A (encode)
    participant B as NA-B (decode + REORDER HOLD)
    participant S as LAN Server

    Note over A,S: THE FIX — B holds the stream at the gap<br/>until the missing chunk is filled

    A->>B: HIT(hash1)
    Note over B: resolves → queue: [1 ready]<br/>front is ready → forward
    B->>S: chunk1 ✓

    A->>B: HIT(hash2)
    Note over B: cannot resolve → queue: [2 HOLE]<br/>fire NAK. front is a HOLE → STOP forwarding
    B-->>A: NAK(hash2)

    A->>B: HIT(hash3)
    Note over B: resolves, BUT front is still a hole →<br/>queue: [2 HOLE][3 ready] — HOLD 3
    A->>B: HIT(hash4)
    Note over B: queue: [2 HOLE][3 ready][4 ready] — HOLD

    A->>B: MISS(chunk2 data)
    Note over B: fills the hole →<br/>queue: [2 ready][3 ready][4 ready]<br/>front now ready → DRAIN in order
    B->>S: chunk2 ✓
    B->>S: chunk3 ✓
    B->>S: chunk4 ✓

    Note over A,S: S received: 1, 2, 3, 4 — CORRECT.<br/>Cost: one round-trip stall while the<br/>hole is filled. Correctness restored.
